      "side": 1,
      "message": "nit: while we are at it, perhaps it\u0027s worth adding a !PAGE_ALIGNED(pvmfw_load_addr) check here as well?\n\nJust to be clear: there is no security issue without it, as `gpa_range_overlaps_pvmfw()` and `pkvm_host_donate_guest()` correctly handle unaligned offsets, and `pkvm_vcpu_pvmfw_entry_init()` sets RIP to `pvmfw_load_addr` correctly.\n\nHowever, a non-page-aligned pvmfw_load_addr causes extra page allocation overhead and an unaligned guest entry point, so enforcing PAGE_ALIGNED(pvmfw_load_addr) would be cleaner API validation. WDYT?\n\n(BTW, I recalled discussing this a while ago and re-checked to confirm if unaligned addresses posed any security issue or not again :) )",
